From: GBRUNCH
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu6: build with DYNAMIC_DEBUG_MODULE

The Android common kernel has DYNAMIC_DEBUG_CORE but not DYNAMIC_DEBUG, so
the IPU6/IPU4P dev_dbg() messages (CSI-2 receiver errors, D-PHY timing,
SOF/EOF events) cannot be enabled at all. Compile the IPU6 objects with
DYNAMIC_DEBUG_MODULE so "insmod intel-ipu6-isys.ko dyndbg=+p" turns them on;
they stay off otherwise.

--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/Makefile
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # GBRUNCH: 7.x allocation helpers on the 6.18 Android common kernel
 ccflags-y += -include $(srctree)/include/media/gbrunch-alloc-compat.h
+# GBRUNCH: dev_dbg() through dynamic debug (dyndbg= module parameter)
+ccflags-y += -DDYNAMIC_DEBUG_MODULE
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 
 intel-ipu6-y			:= ipu6.o \
